{"name":"Mars Red","hex":"#c92a37","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mars","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of mar"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of mar"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mars"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mars Red","blocks":[{"text":"Mars Red is a Japanese anime television series produced by Signal.MD. It is based on a stage reading play written by Bun-O Fujisawa. The series aired from April to June 2021."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/31/MARS_RED_Key_Visual.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars_Red","wikidata":"Q84706088"},{"title":"Mars","blocks":[{"text":"Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun. It is also known as the \"Red Planet\", for its orange-red appearance. Mars is a desert-like rocky planet with a tenuous atmosphere that is primarily carbon dioxide. At the average surface level the atmospheric pressure is a few thousandths of Earth's, atmospheric temperature ranges from −153 to 20 °C, and cosmic radiation is high. Mars retains some water, in the ground as well as thinly in the atmosphere, forming cirrus clouds, fog, frost, larger polar regions of permafrost and ice caps, but no bodies of liquid surface water. Its surface gravity is roughly a third of Earth's or double that of the Moon. Its mean diameter, 6,779 km (4,212 mi), is about half the Earth's, or twice the Moon's, and its surface area is around the size of all the dry land of Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Mars_-_August_30_2021_-_Flickr_-_Kevin_M._Gill.png/330px-Mars_-_August_30_2021_-_Flickr_-_Kevin_M._Gill.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mars","wikidata":"Q111"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red","wikidata":"Q3142"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png/500px-Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png/500px-Terrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mars depicted to scale alongside the planetary-mass objects of the Inner Solar System. From left: Mercury, Venus, Earth, the Moon, Mars and Ceres.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATerrestrial_planet_size_comp_2024.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Olympus_Mons_-_ESA_Mars_Express_-_Flickr_-_Andrea_Luck.png/500px-Olympus_Mons_-_ESA_Mars_Express_-_Flickr_-_Andrea_Luck.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Olympus_Mons_-_ESA_Mars_Express_-_Flickr_-_Andrea_Luck.png/1280px-Olympus_Mons_-_ESA_Mars_Express_-_Flickr_-_Andrea_Luck.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/Olympus_Mons_-_ESA_Mars_Express_-_Flickr_-_Andrea_Luck.png/500px-Olympus_Mons_-_ESA_Mars_Express_-_Flickr_-_Andrea_Luck.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Picture of the tallest volcano on Mars, Olympus Mons. It is approximately 550 km (340 mi) across.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOlympus_Mons_-_ESA_Mars_Express_-_Flickr_-_Andrea_Luck.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/PlanetMars-VallesMarineris-VikingOrbiter-1980.jpg/500px-PlanetMars-VallesMarineris-VikingOrbiter-1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/PlanetMars-VallesMarineris-VikingOrbiter-1980.jpg/1280px-PlanetMars-VallesMarineris-VikingOrbiter-1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/PlanetMars-VallesMarineris-VikingOrbiter-1980.jpg/500px-PlanetMars-VallesMarineris-VikingOrbiter-1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Valles Marineris, taken by the Viking 1 probe","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlanetMars-VallesMarineris-VikingOrbiter-1980.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Geysers_on_Mars.jpg/500px-Geysers_on_Mars.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnai